.TH KAGI-INSTALL 1 "November 2026" "Kagi 0.39.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-install \- stage Kagi node configuration and identity files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts/kagi-install
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run this helper as root from a Kagi source or package tree.
It looks for prebuilt
.BR kagi-cluster-host ,
.BR kagi-host ,
.BR kagi-config ,
and
.B kagi-run
binaries in the tree root and requires
.B kagi-cluster-host
on the executable search path.
If the tree includes manual pages, the helper copies them to
.IR $PREFIX/share/man/man1/ .
.PP
The helper creates the configuration and data directories and writes
.IR $ETC/node.yaml .
It replaces any existing file at that path.
It generates missing ML-DSA-87 identity files and uses the supplied admission
credentials or creates new ones.
The generated YAML contains a one-host, one-disk topology scaffold.
Complete the topology and transport configuration before serving traffic.
The runtime requires at least six hosts and six disks per host.
.PP
If the package includes a
.I kagi-host.service
unit in the tree root, the helper installs it and attempts to enable and start
it.
The optional SSH bootstrap also attempts to add each remote node to Raft.
That operation requires a working cluster and the current leader.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-non-interactive
Skip the prompt for additional SSH targets.
Explicit remote specifications still run.
.TP
.BI \-\-node-id " ID"
Set the node ID.
The default is the short hostname.
.TP
.BI \-\-site " SITE"
Set the failure-domain site.
The default is
.BR site-a .
.TP
.BI \-\-rack " RACK"
Set the failure-domain rack.
The default is
.BR rack-a .
.TP
.BI \-\-endpoint " URL"
Set the node endpoint advertised to peers.
The default uses the first address reported by
.B hostname \-I
and the configured port.
.TP
.BI \-\-remote " user@host,node,site,rack,endpoint"
Attempt to bootstrap a remote node over SSH.
Repeat the option for additional nodes.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR PREFIX ", " ETC ", " DATA
Installation, configuration, and state paths.
Defaults are
.IR /usr/local ,
.IR /etc/kagi ,
and
.IR /var/lib/kagi .
.TP
.B PORT
Local API listen port.
The default is 7400.
.TP
.BR NODE_ID ", " SITE ", " RACK ", " ENDPOINT
Defaults for the corresponding options.
.TP
.BR JOIN_KEY_B64 ", " JOIN_KEY_HASH ", " METADATA_KEY_B64
Admission and metadata credentials.
OpenSSL generates missing keys.
The helper uses
.B b3sum
to derive the admission hash unless
.B JOIN_KEY_HASH
is set.
.TP
.BR LEADER_ID ", " LEADER_ENDPOINT ", " LEADER_PQ_PUB
Leader identity, URL, and public key file for a joining node.
.PP
Use trusted SSH hosts for bootstrap and protect temporary credentials and
generated private keys.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kagi-cluster-host (1),
.BR kagi-config (1),
.BR kagi-tls-cert (1)
